From: OpenMPTCProuter <noreply@openmptcprouter.com>
Subject: fix ndpi_init_detection_module() call for newer bundled libnDPI

The pinned nDPId source (commit 84285ae) still calls the pre-license-type
1-argument form of ndpi_init_detection_module(). The bundled libnDPI pin
(NDPI_COMMIT_HASH, fetched at build time by scripts/get-and-build-libndpi.sh)
has since gained a required `enum ndpi_license_type` second argument
(ntop/nDPI commit 0041f29ef07a578e6cd245a1845d84f179fa3d3b and later),
which breaks the cross build with:

    error: too few arguments to function 'ndpi_init_detection_module'

Pass NDPI_LICENSE_NON_COMMERCIAL_LGPL, matching what nDPI's own tools
(example/ndpiReader.c, example/reader_util.c) and library internals
(src/lib/ndpi_main.c) use as their default/non-commercial license value.

--- a/nDPId.c
+++ b/nDPId.c
@@ -1594,7 +1594,7 @@
     }
 #endif
 
-    workflow->ndpi_struct = ndpi_init_detection_module(global_context);
+    workflow->ndpi_struct = ndpi_init_detection_module(global_context, NDPI_LICENSE_NON_COMMERCIAL_LGPL);
     if (workflow->ndpi_struct == NULL)
     {
         logger_early(1, "%s", "BUG: Could not init ndpi detection module");
